.TH SDL_Semaphore 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_Semaphore \- A means to manage access to a resource, by count, between threads.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_mutex.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_Semaphore SDL_Semaphore;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Semaphores (specifically, \(dqcounting semaphores\(dq), let X number of threads request access at the same time, each thread granted access decrementing a counter\[char46] When the counter reaches zero, future requests block until a prior thread releases their request, incrementing the counter again\[char46]
.PP
Wikipedia has a thorough explanation of the concept:
.PP
https://en\[char46]wikipedia\[char46]org/wiki/Semaphore_(programming)

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

